id=b1051c-launcher3
name=Launcher3 taskbar: transparent on the home screen + spray-paint nav buttons
version=0.2.7
versionCode=9
author=matanmi12
description=Launcher3QuickStep (GSI build bf92e8d5…) + org.b1051c.l3.HomeBg: the 3-button nav row has no background while the default home app (Lawnchair) is on top, and keeps it in apps. Signed with the AOSP testkey like the original. Switch: settings put secure b1051c_taskbar_home_bg 0 (stock look). Spray-paint back / home / recents / all apps (owner artwork, private) + pure black taskbar in apps in Dark theme: static overlay org.b1051c.overlay.launcher3nav (product/overlay/B1051cNavOverlay.apk; off: cmd overlay disable org.b1051c.overlay.launcher3nav). Long-press fix: a long-press on a taskbar app no longer crashes Launcher3 while Lawnchair is home (each taskbar gets its own initialised TaskbarUIController instead of the shared DEFAULT). Recents fix: the taskbar (all apps) no longer stays hidden after Recents -> Home (off: settings put secure b1051c_taskbar_unstash 0). Recents: a "Clear all" button in the action row next to Screenshot / Split, there as soon as Recents opens (org.b1051c.l3.ClearAllAction; off: settings put secure b1051c_recents_clear_all 0). Disable this module + reboot to get the untouched Launcher3 back. Source: work/launcher3patch.
updateJson=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/matanmi12/bigme-b1051c-android16/main/rom/updates/b1051c-launcher3.json
